From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:40:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] nvme-pci: apple-ans: Check the HMB before writing to the
 controller
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The ANS controller needs a host memory buffer that the boot loader
reserved and the NVMMU maps through its SART window. The glue looked it
up only after it had written the controller's configuration space and
cleared CC.EN, so a kernel started by a loader that doesn't fill
/reserved-memory/nvme-hmb stopped the controller and then gave up.

Look the HMB up first, using only register reads, and leave the
controller alone if there is none.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux 39b99e01 (J71t ledger 3.3); only the
 ordering and an error message; the DART-mapped HMB fallback
 (nvme.apple_ans_dart_hmb) is not needed, Orchard's m1n1 fills nvme-hmb
 from the ADT nvme-mmu0 sart-region on every device]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/nvme/host/pci-apple-ans.c | 25 +++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/nvme/host/pci-apple-ans.c b/drivers/nvme/host/pci-apple-ans.c
index a949f7e43..10496dff0 100644
--- a/drivers/nvme/host/pci-apple-ans.c
+++ b/drivers/nvme/host/pci-apple-ans.c
@@ -233,15 +233,26 @@ static int nvme_pci_apple_ans_preinit(struct nvme_dev *dev)
 	if (!ans)
 		return 0;
 
-	ret = nvme_pci_apple_ans_config(dev);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
-
 	core_mask = readl(dev->bar + APPLE_ANS_REG_CORE_MASK);
 	log_size = readl(dev->bar + APPLE_ANS_REG_LOG_SIZE);
 	hmb_size = readl(dev->bar + APPLE_ANS_REG_HMB_SIZE_REQ);
 	hmb_align = readl(dev->bar + APPLE_ANS_REG_HMB_ALIGN_REQ);
 
+	/*
+	 * Check what the controller needs from the boot loader before writing
+	 * anything to it: without a usable HMB, leave it as the loader left it.
+	 */
+	if (!ans->hmb_size) {
+		ret = nvme_pci_apple_ans_find_hmb(dev, hmb_size, hmb_align);
+		if (ret)
+			return dev_err_probe(dev->dev, ret,
+					     "no usable ANS host memory buffer\n");
+	}
+
+	ret = nvme_pci_apple_ans_config(dev);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	writel(0, dev->bar + NVME_REG_CC);
 	ret = readl_poll_timeout(dev->bar + NVME_REG_CSTS, csts,
 				 !(csts & (NVME_CSTS_RDY | NVME_CSTS_CFS)),
@@ -249,12 +260,6 @@ static int nvme_pci_apple_ans_preinit(struct nvme_dev *dev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	if (!ans->hmb_size) {
-		ret = nvme_pci_apple_ans_find_hmb(dev, hmb_size, hmb_align);
-		if (ret)
-			return ret;
-	}
-
 	ret = nvme_pci_apple_ans_reset_dma(dev);
 	if (ret)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev->dev, ret,
